## Timing seam (single point)

All clock access in the probe goes through ONE seam function,
`clock_pair_diff_us` in tests/bench/main.mbt:

    fn clock_pair_diff_us() -> Double {
      let t0 = @core_bench.monotonic_clock_start()
      @core_bench.monotonic_clock_end(t0)
    }

Seam API: @core_bench.monotonic_clock_start() -> Timestamp /
          @core_bench.monotonic_clock_end(Timestamp) -> Double
          (package moonbitlang/core/bench, elapsed returned in microseconds).
No backend branching exists anywhere else in the probe; the only per-backend
file content is the self-identification label (clock_native.mbt / clock_js.mbt
/ clock_wasm.mbt, mapped per target via moon.pkg options(targets: ...), the
same mechanism core/bench itself uses).

Underlying per-backend clock implementations (verified in this machine's
~/.moon/lib/core/bench/monotonic_clock_{native,js,wasm}.mbt):
  native: extern "C" moonbit_monotonic_clock_start / moonbit_monotonic_clock_stop
  js:     extern "js" performance.now()  (elapsed = (now - ts) * 1000.0 us)
  wasm:   "__moonbit_time_unstable" instant_now / instant_elapsed_as_secs_f64

